  "problem": "Price previews could collapse gross charges, discounted cash prices, negotiated amounts and allowed amounts into one comparable measure. Algorithm, percentage and per-diem values could be treated as dollar prices. Missing or negative/zero values could be dropped or treated as valid prices. A passing sample could be treated as legal compliance, complete hospital reporting or comparable patient costs. An obsolete generic MRF schema could replace current pinned CMS definitions.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Price-semantics lives in packages/connectors/mrf/price-semantics.mjs because identity is WP7-sealed. Gross, cash, negotiated and allowed-amount remain different measures. Algorithm, percentage and per-diem values remain non-comparable. Missing or negative/zero values are investigated by documented semantics, not universally dropped or treated as valid prices. A passing sample does not imply legal compliance, complete hospital reporting or comparable patient costs. Current pinned CMS hospital v3.0.0 and payer TiC v2.2.1 definitions are used. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
